		},
		{
			"id": "TPY9EgeqHgLOfWF9g",
			"name": "Butcher's Nails",
			"local_notes": "Requires the Mark of Khorne. The Mark already gives High Pain Threshold, Berserk 12 and Bloodlust 12, so those are not repeated here; this lens is the Battle Rage upgrade and the nails' other effects. A Heretic Astartes who already took Callous from that lens skips this Callous.\n\nLore: Khorne Berzerkers have nails and cables driven into their brains by psycho-surgery, scarring the tissues that handle pain and restraint. Codex: Chaos Space Marines background and Black Library's World Eaters fiction describe warriors who carry on with wounds that would end anyone else, and cannot do anything but kill. The nails are a surgical upgrade to the Blood God's own Mark, not a substitute for it.\n\nDesign: Berserk with Battle Rage (+50%) is -10 x 1.5 = -15; the Mark pays -10, so the nails add -5. Extra Attack 1 (B53) 25, the frenzy the fiction gives Berzerkers (user direction: without it five Berzerkers won 9 fights in 40 against five Marines, losing on damage output, not on defence; with it they win 47 in 60). Hard to Subdue 3 (B59, 2/level) 6. Callous (B125) -5. Bloodlust and High Pain Threshold are left to the Mark. Net -5 + 25 + 6 - 5 = 21 points. Callous overlaps the Heretic Astartes lens; take one.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Disadvantage",
				"Physical",
				"Mental",
				"Chaos",
				"Khorne",
				"Khorne Berzerker",
				"Implant"
			],
			"container_type": "meta_trait",
			"children": [
				{
					"id": "td2iQij63hDi9iyDz",
					"name": "Berserk (Battle Rage upgrade)",
					"reference": "B124",
					"local_notes": "Takes the Mark's Berserk 12 (-10) up to Berserk 12 with the Battle Rage enhancement (+50%, -15 in all). In Battle Rage the bearer keeps the +2 to hit and the other Battle Rage effects while berserk, as on B124. Adds only the difference, -5.",
					"tags": [
						"Disadvantage",
						"Mental"
					],
					"base_points": -5,
					"cr": 12
				},
				{
					"id": "t0kzf5Z-mwK2AXrLo",
					"name": "Extra Attack (Butcher's Nails)",
					"reference": "B53",
					"local_notes": "One more blow a turn, the nails' frenzy: a Berzerker hacks twice where a Marine strikes once.",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Physical"
					],
					"points_per_level": 25,
					"can_level": true,
					"levels": 1,
					"base_points": 0
				},
				{
					"id": "t8GXX3DP8Hpp5rFTH",
					"name": "Hard to Subdue",
					"reference": "B59",
					"local_notes": "+3 to HT rolls to stay conscious. Fights on at 0 HP or stunned when a normal man would fall.",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Physical"
					],
					"points_per_level": 2,
					"can_level": true,
					"levels": 3,
					"base_points": 0
				},
				{
					"id": "tMQFCzwfvYxGxZmwB",
					"name": "Callous",
					"reference": "B125",
					"local_notes": "The nails take pity along with pain.",
					"tags": [
						"Disadvantage",
						"Mental"
					],
					"base_points": -5
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"id": "T-RC8NJDOAFC9uIav",
			"name": "Nurgle's Gift (Plague Marine)",
			"local_notes": "Requires the Mark of Nurgle. The Mark already gives Injury Tolerance (Damage Reduction) 2; the Gift does not add a level, so a Plague Marine's divisor stays 2, as the framework says. Plague Marine DX 16 and HT 16 are adjusted in the template, not here.\n\nLore: Plague Marines are Death Guard and their followers whose bodies have rotted and swollen under Nurgle's care. Codex: Chaos Space Marines background shows armour grown into flesh and bloated, sagging bodies that shrug off bolts. They move slowly and keep on moving.\n\nDesign: Damage Resistance 10 (B46, 5/level) = 50. Reduced Basic Move -2 (B17, -5/level) = -10. Injury Tolerance is not stacked: the Mark's divisor 2 already makes up the framework total. 50 - 10 = 40 points.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Disadvantage",
				"Physical",
				"Chaos",
				"Nurgle",
				"Plague Marine"
			],
			"container_type": "meta_trait",
			"children": [
				{
					"id": "tRG_vGE97kfxkuZtF",
					"name": "Damage Resistance (Fused Rotting Flesh)",
					"reference": "B46",
					"local_notes": "DR 10, all locations. Stacks with worn armour. The plate is fused to the flesh, so it is not removed.",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Physical"
					],
					"points_per_level": 5,
					"can_level": true,
					"levels": 10,
					"base_points": 0,
					"features": [
						{
							"type": "dr_bonus",
							"locations": [
								"all"
							],
							"amount": 10
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"id": "t84YoB4v3e8AX7PX-",
					"name": "Reduced Basic Move (Nurgle's Gift)",
					"reference": "B17",
					"local_notes": "Basic Move -2 (Move 12 to 10 for an Astartes with Move 12).",
					"tags": [
						"Disadvantage",
						"Physical"
					],
					"points_per_level": -5,
					"can_level": true,
					"levels": 2,
					"base_points": 0,
					"features": [
						{
							"type": "attribute_bonus",
							"attribute": "basic_move",
							"amount": -2
						}
					]
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"id": "TFN9Pi641L5X36cei",
			"name": "Rubric of Ahriman (Rubric Marine)",
			"local_notes": "Apply to a raw Astartes (the package without Personal Advancement). It replaces the living organs: the bearer is a sealed suit of Mk IV filled with the dust of its soul. The Astartes organ traits are not removed in the data (the schema cannot delete another entry's children); the GM ignores blood, breath, hunger, sleep and disease. The Rubric's Mk IV plate is part of its equipment. HT 15 for the framework table is a template adjustment.\n\nLore: The Rubric of Ahriman, cast by Ahriman of the Thousand Sons at the Council of Nikaea's end, turned the Legion's mutating warriors to dust inside their own armour; the dust still walks, driven by the Sorcerers' will. Codex: Chaos Space Marines background and the Horus Heresy fiction on the Thousand Sons describe empty suits with ash-soul cores obeying without thought, indifferent to wounds that would kill a living body.\n\nDesign: Attribute Modifiers -120 + Machine Body (Rubric Shell) 85 + Rubric Mind -25 + All Is Dust 20 = -40 points. Unliving is used with No Brain as well as No Blood and No Vitals, matching the framework's list (No Blood, No Brain, No Vitals, Unliving). Doesn't Breathe (B49) 20; Doesn't Eat or Drink (B50) 10; Doesn't Sleep (B50) 20; Unfazeable (B95) 15; Slave Mentality (B154) -40.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Disadvantage",
				"Physical",
				"Mental",
				"Chaos",
				"Tzeentch",
				"Rubric Marine"
			],
			"container_type": "meta_trait",
			"children": [
				{
					"id": "tyXCbZGnOE9NMda1E",
					"name": "Attribute Modifiers (Rubric Marine)",
					"local_notes": "Design: Decreased DX -1 (B15, 20/level, -20) from the Astartes package's 15 for DX 14; Decreased IQ -4 (B16, 20/level, -80) for IQ 6; Reduced Basic Move -4 (B17, 5/level, -20) for Move 8 down from the Astartes 12. -20 - 80 - 20 = -120.",
					"tags": [
						"Physical",
						"Mental"
					],
					"base_points": -120,
					"features": [
						{
							"type": "attribute_bonus",
							"attribute": "dx",
							"amount": -1
						},
						{
							"type": "attribute_bonus",
							"attribute": "iq",
							"amount": -4
						},
						{
							"type": "attribute_bonus",
							"attribute": "basic_move",
							"amount": -4
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"id": "T1SI7vBQPe3wE6UVA",
					"name": "Machine Body (Rubric Shell)",
					"local_notes": "Named \"Machine Body (Rubric Shell)\" so the combat simulator gives a Rubric no FP to spend, as for a Machine: a Rubric has no fatigue.\n\nDesign: 35 (Injury Tolerance) + 20 + 10 + 20 = 85 points.",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Physical"
					],
					"container_type": "meta_trait",
					"children": [
						{
							"id": "tQEyRHrqPcVjIW1bk",
							"name": "Injury Tolerance (Unliving, No Blood, No Brain, No Vitals)",
							"reference": "B60",
							"local_notes": "Unliving wound multipliers (imp and pi++ x1, pi+ x1/2, pi x1/3, pi- x1/5); does not bleed; hits to the vitals or groin count as hits to the torso; a hit to the skull or eye gets no extra effect.",
							"tags": [
								"Advantage",
								"Physical"
							],
							"modifiers": [
								{
									"id": "m-9Ha8jk-c_rl8qX4",
									"name": "Unliving",
									"reference": "B61",
									"cost_adj": "20"
								},
								{
									"id": "mgG2GuQCr-NHYUyXy",
									"name": "No Blood",
									"reference": "B61",
									"cost_adj": "5"
								},
								{
									"id": "m_nXC5mf6v16WRXEC",
									"name": "No Brain",
									"reference": "B61",
									"cost_adj": "5"
								},
								{
									"id": "mmlFK2C-e1c1gLtyD",
									"name": "No Vitals",
									"reference": "B61",
									"cost_adj": "5"
								}
							]
						},
						{
							"id": "t8OlyaqHsgHsKCr0b",
							"name": "Doesn't Breathe",
							"reference": "B49",
							"tags": [
								"Advantage",
								"Physical"
							],
							"base_points": 20
						},
						{
							"id": "tQ8d2n8Os08bQD2lX",
							"name": "Doesn't Eat or Drink",
							"reference": "B50",
							"tags": [
								"Advantage",
